1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:04,567
Over the last four videos, we have met two fields.

2
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:07,407
The electric field is made by charge.

3
00:00:07,427 --> 00:00:11,217
Its lines begin on positive charge and end on negative.

4
00:00:11,627 --> 00:00:15,047
It pushes on any charge, whether that charge is moving

5
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:16,167
or not.

6
00:00:16,187 --> 00:00:19,447
It is the field between the plates of a capacitor.

7
00:00:19,467 --> 00:00:23,087
The magnetic field is made by charge in motion.

8
00:00:23,107 --> 00:00:26,007
Its lines have no beginning and no end.

9
00:00:26,027 --> 00:00:29,087
It pushes only on charge that is moving.

10
00:00:29,107 --> 00:00:32,247
It is the field in and around a coil.

11
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:35,847
So far, the only thing connecting them is charge.

12
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:37,927
A charge makes one field.

13
00:00:37,947 --> 00:00:41,047
Set it moving, and it makes the other as well.

14
00:00:41,067 --> 00:00:43,207
But here is a deeper question.

15
00:00:43,227 --> 00:00:45,847
Can the fields act on each other directly,

16
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:47,527
with no charge in between?

17
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:50,034
Can one field make the other?

18
00:00:50,054 --> 00:00:52,807
The answer took thirty years to find.

19
00:00:52,827 --> 00:00:56,967
It explains how a phone charges on a pad without any contacts,

20
00:00:56,987 --> 00:00:59,367
how a radio signal crosses an ocean,

21
00:00:59,387 --> 00:01:01,617
and what light actually is.

22
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:06,627
The first half of the answer came from Michael Faraday.

23
00:01:06,647 --> 00:01:10,387
Once Oersted had shown that electricity makes magnetism,

24
00:01:10,407 --> 00:01:13,587
Faraday was sure the reverse must be possible.

25
00:01:13,607 --> 00:01:18,387
He wrote himself a note: convert magnetism into electricity.

26
00:01:18,407 --> 00:01:20,547
It took him ten years.

27
00:01:20,567 --> 00:01:22,627
In August of eighteen thirty-one,

28
00:01:22,647 --> 00:01:26,067
he wound two separate coils on an iron ring.

29
00:01:26,087 --> 00:01:27,614
One went to a battery.

30
00:01:27,634 --> 00:01:29,560
The other went to a meter.

31
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:31,934
There was no connection between them.

32
00:01:31,954 --> 00:01:34,254
With a steady current in the first coil,

33
00:01:34,274 --> 00:01:36,547
the meter showed nothing at all.

34
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:38,747
That was why everyone had failed.

35
00:01:38,767 --> 00:01:41,267
They had been looking for a steady effect.

36
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:44,627
But Faraday noticed that at the instant he switched the

37
00:01:44,647 --> 00:01:47,027
current on, the needle kicked.

38
00:01:47,047 --> 00:01:48,574
Then it settled back.

39
00:01:48,594 --> 00:01:51,774
And when he switched off, it kicked the other way.

40
00:01:51,794 --> 00:01:54,547
You can see the same thing with a bar magnet and a coil

41
00:01:54,567 --> 00:01:55,587
of wire.

42
00:01:55,607 --> 00:01:58,467
Push the magnet in, and a current flows.

43
00:01:58,487 --> 00:02:00,814
Hold it still, however strong it is,

44
00:02:00,834 --> 00:02:02,267
and nothing happens.

45
00:02:02,287 --> 00:02:05,374
Pull it out, and the current flows the other way.

46
00:02:05,394 --> 00:02:08,227
A steady magnetic field does nothing.

47
00:02:08,247 --> 00:02:11,187
Only a changing one drives a current.

48
00:02:11,207 --> 00:02:13,347
Now think about what that means.

49
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:16,307
The charges in that wire were sitting at rest,

50
00:02:16,327 --> 00:02:18,334
and something pushed them.

51
00:02:18,354 --> 00:02:21,587
A magnetic field cannot push a charge at rest.

52
00:02:21,607 --> 00:02:23,827
Only an electric field can.

53
00:02:23,847 --> 00:02:28,507
So a changing magnetic field must create an electric field.

54
00:02:28,527 --> 00:02:31,534
And it is an electric field of a new kind.

55
00:02:31,554 --> 00:02:35,117
The fields we met before start on one charge and end on

56
00:02:35,407 --> 00:02:36,027
another.

57
00:02:36,047 --> 00:02:39,347
This one has no charges to start or end on.

58
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:42,307
Its lines close on themselves, in loops,

59
00:02:42,327 --> 00:02:44,707
circling the changing magnetic field.

60
00:02:44,727 --> 00:02:47,027
The wire only reveals it.

61
00:02:47,047 --> 00:02:49,987
Take the wire away, and the loops of electric field are

62
00:02:50,007 --> 00:02:52,387
still there, in empty space.

63
00:02:52,407 --> 00:02:54,227
You may have this in your kitchen.

64
00:02:54,247 --> 00:02:57,587
Under the glass of an induction cooker is a coil carrying

65
00:02:57,607 --> 00:02:59,720
a rapidly changing current.

66
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:02,974
Its changing magnetic field passes up through the glass,

67
00:03:02,994 --> 00:03:05,837
and creates loops of electric field in the base of the

68
00:03:06,087 --> 00:03:06,547
pan.

69
00:03:06,567 --> 00:03:08,574
Those drive currents in the metal,

70
00:03:08,594 --> 00:03:10,654
and the pan heats itself.

71
00:03:10,674 --> 00:03:13,707
The glass stays cool, because there is nothing in glass

72
00:03:13,727 --> 00:03:15,357
for the field to push around.

73
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:19,593
Faraday was a brilliant experimenter,

74
00:03:19,613 --> 00:03:22,163
but he had almost no mathematics.

75
00:03:22,653 --> 00:03:26,633
Thirty years later, a Scottish physicist named James Clerk

76
00:03:26,653 --> 00:03:31,163
Maxwell set out to turn Faraday's pictures into equations.

77
00:03:31,293 --> 00:03:33,833
He wrote down everything that was known,

78
00:03:33,853 --> 00:03:37,323
and he found that the rules did not quite fit together.

79
00:03:37,453 --> 00:03:40,003
The trouble showed up in a capacitor.

80
00:03:40,173 --> 00:03:42,483
Think of a capacitor being charged.

81
00:03:42,573 --> 00:03:45,833
Current flows along the wire, and around the wire there

82
00:03:45,853 --> 00:03:50,083
is a magnetic field, in rings, exactly as Oersted found.

83
00:03:50,413 --> 00:03:52,643
Now follow the wire to the plate.

84
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:54,963
Between the plates there is a gap.

85
00:03:55,053 --> 00:03:56,603
No charge crosses it.

86
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,603
There is no current there at all.

87
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:01,043
So what happens to the magnetic field?

88
00:04:01,293 --> 00:04:03,913
Does it simply stop, at the edge of the plate,

89
00:04:03,933 --> 00:04:05,683
and start again on the other side?

90
00:04:06,013 --> 00:04:08,243
A field cannot be cut off like that.

91
00:04:08,573 --> 00:04:10,763
But look at what is in the gap.

92
00:04:10,813 --> 00:04:12,163
It is not empty.

93
00:04:12,253 --> 00:04:15,433
As the plates charge, the electric field between them

94
00:04:15,453 --> 00:04:18,123
is growing stronger every instant.

95
00:04:18,253 --> 00:04:21,003
Maxwell proposed that this is enough.

96
00:04:21,053 --> 00:04:24,153
A changing electric field makes a magnetic field around

97
00:04:24,173 --> 00:04:26,243
it, just as a current does.

98
00:04:26,333 --> 00:04:29,793
With that one addition, the rings of magnetic field carry

99
00:04:29,813 --> 00:04:33,033
on smoothly around the gap, and the rules fit together

100
00:04:33,053 --> 00:04:34,043
everywhere.

101
00:04:34,173 --> 00:04:36,443
Nobody had ever seen this effect.

102
00:04:36,493 --> 00:04:40,003
It is far too small to detect with a compass and a capacitor.

103
00:04:40,253 --> 00:04:43,753
Maxwell added it because the mathematics demanded it,

104
00:04:43,773 --> 00:04:46,483
and because of what it led to next.

105
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:50,303
Now put the two halves side by side.

106
00:04:50,633 --> 00:04:54,183
A changing magnetic field makes an electric field.

107
00:04:54,313 --> 00:04:57,783
A changing electric field makes a magnetic field.

108
00:04:57,913 --> 00:04:59,463
Do you see what follows?

109
00:04:59,593 --> 00:05:01,743
Take a charge and give it a shake.

110
00:05:01,993 --> 00:05:04,103
Its electric field changes.

111
00:05:04,233 --> 00:05:07,263
That change makes a magnetic field around it.

112
00:05:07,433 --> 00:05:10,613
But a moment ago that magnetic field was not there,

113
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:12,463
so it is changing too.

114
00:05:12,553 --> 00:05:15,853
And a changing magnetic field makes an electric field,

115
00:05:15,873 --> 00:05:17,263
a little further out.

116
00:05:17,353 --> 00:05:21,093
Which is new, and changing, and so makes a magnetic field

117
00:05:21,113 --> 00:05:22,223
beyond that.

118
00:05:22,313 --> 00:05:25,893
It is like a row of dominoes, where each one falling tips

119
00:05:25,913 --> 00:05:26,783
the next.

120
00:05:26,873 --> 00:05:29,343
Except that here there are no dominoes.

121
00:05:29,753 --> 00:05:33,333
Each field creates the other, one step further on,

122
00:05:33,353 --> 00:05:34,703
in empty space.

123
00:05:34,793 --> 00:05:37,733
So the disturbance does not stay near the charge.

124
00:05:37,753 --> 00:05:40,223
It travels outward by itself.

125
00:05:40,313 --> 00:05:43,983
The charge can stop moving, and the ripple carries on.

126
00:05:44,153 --> 00:05:48,423
Maxwell had found, on paper, an electromagnetic wave.

127
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:50,263
It has a particular shape.

128
00:05:50,393 --> 00:05:53,413
Flick a rope, and the rope moves up and down while the

129
00:05:53,433 --> 00:05:54,863
hump travels along.

130
00:05:55,113 --> 00:05:58,413
In the same way, the electric field in the wave points

131
00:05:58,433 --> 00:06:00,143
across the direction of travel.

132
00:06:00,393 --> 00:06:02,933
The magnetic field points across it too,

133
00:06:02,953 --> 00:06:05,223
at right angles to the electric field.

134
00:06:05,273 --> 00:06:07,733
And the two rise and fall together,

135
00:06:07,753 --> 00:06:08,543
in step.

136
00:06:08,873 --> 00:06:10,933
Unlike the hump on a rope, though,

137
00:06:10,953 --> 00:06:13,383
this wave needs nothing to travel in.

138
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:15,663
The fields carry themselves.

139
00:06:17,033 --> 00:06:19,263
How fast does such a wave travel?

140
00:06:19,673 --> 00:06:23,423
Maxwell could work it out, and he needed only two numbers.

141
00:06:23,753 --> 00:06:25,423
We have already met both.

142
00:06:25,753 --> 00:06:28,783
The first appeared in the formula for a capacitor.

143
00:06:28,873 --> 00:06:32,853
It tells us how strong the electric field of a given charge

144
00:06:32,873 --> 00:06:33,543
is.

145
00:06:33,753 --> 00:06:36,623
The second appeared in the formula for a coil.

146
00:06:36,953 --> 00:06:40,693
It tells us how strong the magnetic field of a given current

147
00:06:40,713 --> 00:06:41,183
is.

148
00:06:41,753 --> 00:06:44,133
Neither has anything to do with waves,

149
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,103
or with speed.

150
00:06:45,513 --> 00:06:48,453
You measure them on a bench, with metal plates,

151
00:06:48,473 --> 00:06:51,383
coils of wire, and a sensitive balance.

152
00:06:51,593 --> 00:06:54,853
Two German physicists, Weber and Kohlrausch,

153
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:58,143
had done exactly that in eighteen fifty-six.

154
00:06:58,313 --> 00:07:01,023
Maxwell put their figures into his equations.

155
00:07:01,353 --> 00:07:05,583
Out came a speed: three hundred and ten thousand kilometres

156
00:07:05,673 --> 00:07:07,143
every second.

157
00:07:07,433 --> 00:07:09,623
He had seen a number like that before.

158
00:07:09,753 --> 00:07:12,106
A few years earlier, in France,

159
00:07:12,126 --> 00:07:15,093
Hippolyte Fizeau had sent a beam of light through the

160
00:07:15,113 --> 00:07:18,453
teeth of a spinning wheel to a mirror eight kilometres

161
00:07:18,473 --> 00:07:21,463
away, and timed its journey there and back.

162
00:07:21,593 --> 00:07:24,573
His result for the speed of light was three hundred and

163
00:07:24,593 --> 00:07:26,783
fifteen thousand kilometres a second.

164
00:07:27,433 --> 00:07:30,303
One number came from charged plates and coils.

165
00:07:30,553 --> 00:07:33,583
The other came from a light beam and a toothed wheel.

166
00:07:33,913 --> 00:07:36,423
They agreed to within two percent.

167
00:07:36,633 --> 00:07:40,063
Maxwell wrote that we can scarcely avoid the conclusion

168
00:07:40,153 --> 00:07:43,423
that light itself is an electromagnetic wave.

169
00:07:43,913 --> 00:07:48,133
Until then, optics, electricity and magnetism had been

170
00:07:48,153 --> 00:07:49,983
three separate sciences.

171
00:07:50,073 --> 00:07:52,463
From that moment, they were one.

172
00:07:53,833 --> 00:07:56,143
But it was still only a prediction.

173
00:07:56,473 --> 00:07:59,103
Maxwell died in eighteen seventy-nine,

174
00:07:59,153 --> 00:08:00,853
without seeing it tested.

175
00:08:00,873 --> 00:08:03,013
The proof came eight years later,

176
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:06,423
from a young German professor, Heinrich Hertz.

177
00:08:06,633 --> 00:08:10,333
If Maxwell was right, then charge rushing back and forth

178
00:08:10,353 --> 00:08:12,133
should send out waves.

179
00:08:12,153 --> 00:08:14,373
So on one side of his laboratory,

180
00:08:14,393 --> 00:08:18,533
Hertz set up two brass rods with a small gap between them,

181
00:08:18,553 --> 00:08:21,653
and made a spark leap back and forth across it,

182
00:08:21,673 --> 00:08:24,213
many millions of times a second.

183
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:27,333
On the other side of the room, he held a simple loop of

184
00:08:27,353 --> 00:08:29,933
wire with a tiny gap of its own.

185
00:08:29,953 --> 00:08:31,813
It was connected to nothing.

186
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:34,053
No battery, no wires.

187
00:08:34,073 --> 00:08:37,733
When the first spark fired, a faint spark appeared in

188
00:08:37,753 --> 00:08:39,253
the gap of the loop.

189
00:08:39,273 --> 00:08:41,613
Something had crossed the room.

190
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:44,693
Hertz went on to test it as you would test light.

191
00:08:44,713 --> 00:08:47,533
A metal sheet reflected it, like a mirror.

192
00:08:47,553 --> 00:08:49,573
A curved one focused it.

193
00:08:49,593 --> 00:08:51,493
And when he measured its speed,

194
00:08:51,513 --> 00:08:53,743
it was the speed of light.

195
00:08:53,793 --> 00:08:56,213
Asked what use his discovery might be,

196
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:59,253
he is said to have replied: none at all.

197
00:08:59,273 --> 00:09:01,013
He was wrong about that.

198
00:09:01,033 --> 00:09:04,543
In nineteen hundred and one, Guglielmo Marconi sent a

199
00:09:04,593 --> 00:09:06,453
signal across the Atlantic.

200
00:09:06,473 --> 00:09:10,133
Today the unit of frequency, one cycle each second,

201
00:09:10,153 --> 00:09:12,013
is called the hertz.

202
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:14,853
Hertz's waves were a few metres long.

203
00:09:14,873 --> 00:09:17,663
Light waves are less than a thousandth of a millimetre

204
00:09:17,873 --> 00:09:18,453
long.

205
00:09:18,473 --> 00:09:21,173
That is the only difference between them.

206
00:09:21,193 --> 00:09:23,813
Radio waves, as long as a building.

207
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:26,133
Microwaves, the size of your hand,

208
00:09:26,153 --> 00:09:28,293
which is why they fit inside an oven.

209
00:09:28,313 --> 00:09:30,960
Infrared, which you feel as warmth.

210
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:33,493
The narrow band that your eyes can detect.

211
00:09:33,513 --> 00:09:34,853
Ultraviolet.

212
00:09:34,873 --> 00:09:37,413
X-rays, smaller than an atom.

213
00:09:37,433 --> 00:09:41,653
They are all the same thing: electric and magnetic fields,

214
00:09:41,673 --> 00:09:45,583
each creating the other, crossing space at the same speed.

215
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:50,557
There is one more step, and it is the strangest.

216
00:09:51,047 --> 00:09:53,277
Picture a charge sitting on a table.

217
00:09:53,607 --> 00:09:55,357
You are standing beside it.

218
00:09:55,767 --> 00:09:58,187
Around it there is an electric field,

219
00:09:58,207 --> 00:10:00,077
and no magnetic field at all.

220
00:10:00,407 --> 00:10:02,717
A compass in your hand does nothing.

221
00:10:03,287 --> 00:10:05,597
Now a friend walks past the table.

222
00:10:05,927 --> 00:10:08,557
From where they are, the charge is moving.

223
00:10:08,887 --> 00:10:12,317
And we learned that a moving charge makes a magnetic field.

224
00:10:12,647 --> 00:10:15,277
So your friend's compass should swing.

225
00:10:15,447 --> 00:10:16,477
Who is right?

226
00:10:16,567 --> 00:10:19,237
Is there a magnetic field or not?

227
00:10:19,687 --> 00:10:20,717
Both are right.

228
00:10:21,127 --> 00:10:24,707
In nineteen hundred and five, Albert Einstein opened his

229
00:10:24,727 --> 00:10:28,237
most famous paper with exactly this puzzle.

230
00:10:28,407 --> 00:10:31,667
His answer was that the electric field and the magnetic

231
00:10:31,687 --> 00:10:34,387
field are not two separate things.

232
00:10:34,407 --> 00:10:36,867
They are two faces of one thing,

233
00:10:36,887 --> 00:10:39,107
the electromagnetic field.

234
00:10:39,127 --> 00:10:41,187
How much of it appears as electric,

235
00:10:41,207 --> 00:10:45,467
and how much as magnetic, depends on how you are moving.

236
00:10:45,487 --> 00:10:47,747
It is a little like looking at a coin.

237
00:10:47,767 --> 00:10:49,987
From the front you see a circle.

238
00:10:50,007 --> 00:10:51,917
From the edge you see a line.

239
00:10:52,247 --> 00:10:54,077
The coin has not changed.

240
00:10:54,167 --> 00:10:55,277
You have.

241
00:10:55,447 --> 00:10:59,277
That is why the two fields are bound so tightly together.

242
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:00,877
They were never really two.

243
00:11:01,687 --> 00:11:04,987
The equations that describe this single field were tidied

244
00:11:05,007 --> 00:11:08,067
into the form we use today by Oliver Heaviside,

245
00:11:08,087 --> 00:11:09,907
in eighteen eighty-four.

246
00:11:09,927 --> 00:11:14,157
He reduced Maxwell's twenty equations to four short lines.

247
00:11:14,487 --> 00:11:17,837
Every electrical machine ever built obeys them.

248
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:23,230
For an engineer, this changes how you look at every circuit.

249
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:25,100
Start with something small.

250
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,740
A wireless charging pad has a coil in it,

251
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,700
carrying a changing current.

252
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:32,460
Your phone has a second coil in its back.

253
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,820
The changing magnetic field of the first creates an electric

254
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,900
field in the second, and drives a current that charges

255
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:39,980
the battery.

256
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,340
Nothing touches.

257
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:44,380
The energy crosses the gap as field.

258
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,580
A transformer is the same idea,

259
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:49,420
built to carry the power of a whole town.

260
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:52,940
Two coils that never touch, linked only by a changing

261
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,420
magnetic field.

262
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:57,020
An antenna goes one step further.

263
00:11:57,040 --> 00:12:00,220
Charge is driven up and down a wire so quickly that its

264
00:12:00,240 --> 00:12:01,900
fields cannot keep up.

265
00:12:01,920 --> 00:12:04,860
They break away and travel off as waves.

266
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:08,380
Far away, a second antenna sits in the passing wave,

267
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:11,340
and the wave's electric field pushes its charges back

268
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,300
and forth.

269
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:15,100
That tiny current is your radio signal.

270
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:18,327
Even in an ordinary cable, the picture changes.

271
00:12:18,347 --> 00:12:21,527
The energy does not really travel inside the copper.

272
00:12:21,547 --> 00:12:25,180
It travels in the fields around and between the two conductors,

273
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:28,220
guided by them, at close to the speed of light.

274
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:31,340
The electrons themselves, as we saw in the first video,

275
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,807
barely crawl.

276
00:12:32,827 --> 00:12:34,860
And that speed, though enormous,

277
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,540
is not infinite.

278
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:40,060
At fifty cycles a second, one wavelength is six thousand

279
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,473
kilometres long.

280
00:12:41,493 --> 00:12:43,420
On a very long transmission line,

281
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:46,780
the voltage at the far end is noticeably out of step with

282
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,673
the voltage at the near end.

283
00:12:48,693 --> 00:12:50,950
Power engineers have to design for that.

284
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:53,810
So let's put it together.

285
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:56,210
Charge makes an electric field.

286
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:59,250
Moving charge makes a magnetic field.

287
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:02,810
A changing magnetic field makes an electric field.

288
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:04,120
That was Faraday.

289
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:07,480
A changing electric field makes a magnetic field.

290
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:08,810
That was Maxwell.

291
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:11,880
Because each makes the other, the two can travel through

292
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,250
empty space together as a wave.

293
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,090
Hertz found that wave.

294
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:17,810
Light is one kind of it.

295
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:21,880
And the two fields are really two faces of one electromagnetic

296
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:22,610
field.

297
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,560
One of those links matters more to an electrical engineer

298
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:30,090
than any other: a changing magnetic field makes a voltage.

299
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:32,880
Next time, in the last video of this series,

300
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:34,560
we take it apart properly.

301
00:13:34,580 --> 00:13:37,080
It is called electromagnetic induction,

302
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:41,160
and it runs every generator and every transformer on Earth.

303
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:44,320
If this helped you see it, and not just calculate it,

304
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:47,250
please like, share, and subscribe to this channel.
